          "linkId": "cl-body",
          "text": "Contact lenses are FDA-regulated medical devices. A contact lens evaluation is separate from a comprehensive eye exam. The fitting fee covers diagnostic lenses and scheduled follow-up visits within the stated window. A prescription is released only after the doctor finds the fit acceptable. Sleeping in lenses (unless a specifically approved extended-wear lens) greatly increases the risk of infection and scarring. Overwear, tap water, and topping off solution are unsafe. State law controls Rx expiration and copy-release.",
          "type": "display"
        },
